# explainer-leave (M11): the pointer leaving the chip closes what its rest opened (a close by the
# pointer ends only what the pointer opened): open on a's chip and at rest, the pointer onto the top
# bar (760, 48), the explainer going back into its caret linearly over 200 ms (Callout.module.css
# [data-closing], dur-overlay-leave), taking no input meanwhile, then gone. Inputs and closing shots
# fall on the 16 ms grid: a closing explainer is gone at its exit's end, React's at that instant,
# the port's from its next frame.
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
wait 2000
move 70 424
wait 1104
move 760 48
shot leave-0000
wait 48
shot leave-0048
wait 48
shot leave-0096
wait 48
shot leave-0144
wait 48
shot leave-0192
wait 16
shot leave-gone
